## 4. Priority 3 — hardening

### 4.1 Connection-pool validation (the recurring 500s)

**CLASS:** FILE CHANGE + PRODUCTION-IMPACTING (needs a restart)

**Status:** not configured.

**Why:** OpenMRS uses c3p0 with **no connection validation**, and MySQL closes connections
idle beyond `wait_timeout` (**28800s = 8h**). After the stack sits idle for days, c3p0 hands
Hibernate dead connections and pages fail with
`Could not open Hibernate Session … JDBC begin transaction failed`. This **already happened
on 2026-08-30** and was cleared by restarting `openmrs-app`. **It will recur.**

Note `connection.url` already carries `autoReconnect=true` — a deprecated MySQL option that
does **not** reliably prevent this and gives false confidence.

**Candidate fix** — add to `/usr/local/tomcat/.OpenMRS/openmrs-runtime.properties`:

```
hibernate.c3p0.preferredTestQuery=SELECT 1
hibernate.c3p0.idleConnectionTestPeriod=300
hibernate.c3p0.testConnectionOnCheckout=true
```

> **Verify rather than assume.** I have not confirmed that this OpenMRS build forwards
> `hibernate.c3p0.*` from the runtime properties to Hibernate. Back the file up, apply,
> restart, and confirm the settings take effect before treating this as fixed.

**Workaround meanwhile:** `docker restart openmrs-app` (~2 minutes).

